Subject: [PATCH] wiki: document the Crumble Control API and its console
 commands

API Reference gains a Gambonanza.CrumbleApi.Crumble section: the one-gambit
example, the three handle kinds (Freeze/Block/Delay) and exactly what each
does to the game's countdown, the direct actions, the reads, the two step
events, and how the library brackets a private method without Harmony by
re-ordering TurnManager.OnPlayerCheckIfCanPlay. Console Commands lists the
`crumble` family under mod-provided commands, and Example Mods points at
CrumbleCore.cs as the reference for the delegate-bracketing pattern.
