+### Crumble Control API
+
+Installed with any gambit that depends on it, and usable on its own:
+
+| Command | What it does |
+| ------- | ------------ |
+| `crumble` | Crumble mode status: countdown, threshold, shaking/fallen tiles, and every API handle with who holds it. |
+| `crumble freeze [on\|off]` | Pause the crumble: no countdown tick, nothing falls, nothing new shakes. |
+| `crumble block [on\|off]` | Crumble mode can never start while on. |
+| `crumble delay <n>` | Set the console's own extra countdown turns to `n` (`0` clears; gambits' delays stack on top). |
+| `crumble start [quiet]` | Begin crumble mode now. `quiet` skips the OnCrumble/influence part. |
+| `crumble stop [keep]` | End crumble mode and settle shaking tiles; `keep` leaves the counter where it is. |
+| `crumble counter <n>` | Set the countdown counter. |
+| `crumble shake` | Shake the game's next batch of tiles now. They fall on the next step while crumble mode is on; otherwise they keep shaking until it starts. |
+| `crumble calm` | Settle every shaking tile without ending crumble mode. |
+
+The console's own freeze/block/delay are separate handles from any gambit's, so
+`crumble freeze off` never releases a card's freeze. Full API:
+[API Reference](API-Reference#gambonanzacrumbleapicrumble).
+
